// The documentation groups whose members are spread over several of this
// library's headers, declared where no header has to include another to
// reach them.

/** @defgroup motion-time Time
 *  The one unit every length, delay, step and period is stated in
 *  (time/Duration.h). */
/** @defgroup motion-clock The clock
 *  The engine animations, timelines and timers run on, the frame that
 *  moves it under a policy, and the held motions a reconciler runs
 *  (clock/Engine.h, advanced/ClockPolicy.h, advanced/Held.h). */
/** @defgroup motion-values Animatable values
 *  How a property changes over time, as values with no renderer in them:
 *  the transition, the keyed track, the spring, the oscillator, the
 *  property that can hold any of them, and the lanes a held motion is
 *  retargeted through (values/Values.h). */
/** @defgroup motion-ease Curves
 *  The curves a motion is shaped by: the one type every curve slot
 *  holds, the named catalogue, the parameterised families, and the rule
 *  two held curves compare by (ease/Ease.h). */
/** @defgroup motion-bind Bindings
 *  One number shaped into another: the stages a followed number runs
 *  through as fields, and the wiggle noise laid over the result
 *  (bind/Binding.h, bind/WiggleNoise.h). */
/** @defgroup motion-schedule Schedules
 *  A value that differs per child, the orderings it deals in, and how a
 *  run of units shares one progress: a timing resolved against a frame's
 *  counts into a beat per unit (schedule/Stagger.h, schedule/Schedule.h). */
/** @defgroup motion-physics Physics
 *  A point set that is stepped rather than read: the lanes a simulation
 *  is, the forces and constraints over them, the grid that answers what
 *  is near what, the Verlet stepper, and particles that are born, age
 *  and die (physics/Points.h, physics/Forces.h, physics/Neighbourhood.h,
 *  physics/Constraints.h, physics/Verlet.h, physics/Particles.h). */
